From 494eedc107cc51f14af0cc73ed5a3c5bba9b3fb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jesse Osiecki <jesse@jjo.ninja>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 12:04:49 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] Add a PipeWire recorder, musl fixes and rubber stamp
 fail-closed fixes

Port for postmarketOS (musl, Plasma Mobile) on a Lenovo IdeaPad Duet 3,
whose cameras are raw MIPI sensors that only exist behind libcamera. No
V4L2 node hands out finished frames and libcamera's v4l2-compat shim
segfaults on musl, so the desktop's PipeWire session is the only way to
get at the front camera.

- recorders/pipewire_reader.py: new recording_plugin "pipewire" using
  GStreamer pipewiresrc -> videoconvert -> appsink, exposing the small
  cv2.VideoCapture-like API compare.py expects. Config keys
  pipewire_target (node name or object.serial) and pipewire_timeout.
  Falls back to the invoking user's /run/user/<uid> under sudo so
  `howdy add` and `howdy test` work from a terminal.
- video_capture.py: skip the device_path existence check for pipewire.
- pam/main.cc: pass environ to posix_spawnp. A null envp is an empty
  environment on musl, so the compare process could not find
  XDG_RUNTIME_DIR and the PipeWire socket.
- pam/meson.build: link libintl; musl keeps gettext separate.
- rubberstamps/nod.py: on timeout return failsafe, not its inverse. A
  faildeadly rule previously approved anyone who simply did not nod.
- rubberstamps/__init__.py: a stamp that crashes under a faildeadly rule
  now exits 15 instead of being skipped (which approved the login), and
  writes to a dead howdy-gtk helper no longer crash the stamp.
